# FleetOps responsive layout

All new pages, forms, tables, and layout changes must work from 320px through desktop.

## Breakpoints (Tailwind v4)

| Token | px | Use for |
|-------|-----|---------|
| `sm` | 640 | 2-col forms/KPIs, show secondary header text |
| `md` | 768 | Table ↔ card list split |
| `lg` | 1024 | Sidebar vs bottom nav, auth split, 2-col dashboards |
| `xl` | 1280 | Dense KPI rows only (5+ columns) |

**Nav boundary is `lg`**, not `md`.

## Required patterns

### Tables
Dual render — never horizontal-scroll-only on mobile:

```tsx
<ul className="divide-y md:hidden">{/* cards */}</ul>
<div className="hidden overflow-x-auto md:block">
  <table className="data-table w-full">…</table>
</div>
```

See `src/routes/fleet.tsx`.

### Multi-column pages
Prefer `lg:grid-cols-[…]` for operational 2-column layouts (dispatch, request detail, dashboards). Reserve `xl:` for 4+ KPI columns.

### Page structure
- Wrap content in `page-stack`
- Forms: `form-grid sm:grid-cols-2`
- KPIs: `<KpiGrid>` or `sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4`
- Use `min-w-0`, `truncate`, `flex-wrap` on headers and toolbars

### Auth
Layout lives in `src/styles.css` (`.auth-split-*`). Below `lg`: hide hero visual, form-only card. Do not animate/pan the whole SVG.

### Shell
`AppShell` handles mobile nav — do not add shadcn `SidebarProvider`. Main content uses `pb-20 lg:pb-4` for bottom nav clearance.

## Checklist before shipping UI

- [ ] Readable at 375px width
- [ ] Touch targets ≥ 44px where tappable
- [ ] No required horizontal scroll for primary actions
- [ ] Header actions wrap (`flex-wrap`)
- [ ] Inputs use `text-base` on mobile (see `styles.css` 640px rule — prevents iOS zoom)
